    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "Both earlier answers are confirmed by their respective captured worked solutions. For q-73531, the extreme value theorem requires continuity on a closed, bounded interval. I contains the infinite discontinuity at x=1; II is not closed; III is closed and avoids x=1. The worked solution mistakenly writes [-1,1] while discussing I=[-2,2], but its answer remains correct. For q-129218, the real domain is x>-2 with x≠2. I includes points outside the domain, III contains x=2, and II is a closed, bounded interval on which the function is continuous.",
